ins (2025) as gone quiet and says Felix is still active. It does not credit Dmitri Volkov with printVersion. The criterion requires that crediting too.\",\"pass\":false}],\"C\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer C gives Felix 37% of 2,246 lines including the generated table, below 40%. It gives about 48% without the table, but the headline is 37% and Wen Li is shown at 25%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer C shows Wen Li at 25%, though it does note that most of it is the generated table. It says help.zig is someone else's code but does not name jnagpaul/Dhole. Wen Li's remaining 68 lines are about 3%, above the limit.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer C gives a bus factor of about 2 using Felix and Wen, not jnagpaul, and says nothing about jnagpaul stopping in 2023. Felix is stated as about 48% without the table, but the bus factor pairing is wrong.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer C gives 37% as the loss and mentions no combined figure with already departed authors.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer C does not list who has left. It only mentions that 11 people committed in the last 12 months and does not name jnagpaul, Vincent Rischmann or mochalins as inactive.\",\"pass\":false}],\"D\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer D gives Felix about 39% of roughly 2,280 lines, which is below 40%. It credits help.zig to Tobias Ek, so it fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer D says help.zig is 100% Tobias Ek, which is the named failure case.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer D gives a bus factor of about 4 (tool says 6), which is 3 or more, so it fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer D gives 39% as the loss and says 9 of 13 files are mostly inactive. It does not give the combined figure of about 85%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer D treats Felix as inactive and gone (no commit in 6 months). It does not name the required departed authors. This is a failure.\",\"pass\":false}],\"E\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer E gives Felix about 37% of 2,225 lines, which is below 40%, and shows Wen Li at 25%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer E shows Wen Li at 25% and the width table counted as owned, although it hedges that it looks generated. It does not make the help.zig attribution statement.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer E says the bus factor is about 2 for the repo, but does not tie it to jnagpaul, and says no part of the code is fully orphaned. It gives Felix at 37%, not in the required range.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer E says 37% would have no author left and does not give a combined figure with departed authors.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer E does not name jnagpaul, Vincent Rischmann or mochalins as having left, and says no part of the code is orphaned. It says Felix is active, which is correct, but the rest is missing.\",\"pass\":false}],\"F\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer F gives Felix 35.8% of 2,120 lines, below 40%, and puts Wen Li at 26%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer F shows Wen Li at 26% and credits the generated width table as written. It does not make the help.zig attribution statement.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer F gives a bus factor of 2 via Felix plus Wen Li, not jnagpaul. Felix is at 35.8%, below the range. It also says Felix has no commits in 90 days, calling him not the current maintainer.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer F says 36% would be lost, or 62% with Wen Li. There is no combined figure with departed authors in the 80-90% range.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer F says Felix is not active, which is the named failure case of describing him as having left. It marks jnagpaul, Vincent and mochalins as inactive in a table, but still fails on Felix.\",\"pass\":false}]}","ttft_ms":16382,"type":"result","duration_ms":16395,"uuid":"9f499da9-c0ce-4883-a1f5-7df527614285","ttft_stream_ms":2106,"time_t